            "count": 0,
            "bug_id": 19238,
            "text": "RestoreToEnv() in src/main/saveload.c only checks that the object a save\nfile unserializes to is headed by a pairlist node, then walks CDR() to\nthe end and takes TAG() and CAR() of every node as a symbol and its\nvalue. A malformed .RData file can put any object in CDR position, and\nits fields are then read as pairlist slots. An external pointer there\n(the fuzzer's input) has a NULL address in its CAR slot, which\ndefineVar() binds and R_seemsOldStyleS4Object() dereferences:\n\n    ==6788==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: SEGV on unknown address 0x000000000000\n        #0 Rf_isObject               src/main/memory.c\n        #1 R_seemsOldStyleS4Object   src/main/objects.c\n        #2 RestoreToEnv              src/main/saveload.c\n        #3 R_LoadSavedData           src/main/saveload.c\n        #4 do_load                   src/main/saveload.c\n\nA vector in that position dereferences NULL through its length fields,\nand a fresh symbol loops forever: its SYMVALUE() is R_UnboundValue,\nwhose own SYMVALUE() is itself. Both load() entry points (loadFromConn2\nand the .Internal(load()) fallback) go through RestoreToEnv(), in\nreleased R as well as R-devel (r90729). Found by OSS-Fuzz (testcase\n4654451810697216).\n\nProposed patch: attached as load-pairlist-chain.diff. The count loop now\nrequires every node to be a LISTSXP with a symbol tag and otherwise\nraises the existing \"loaded data is not in pair list form\" error. A\nregression test in tests/reg-tests-1e.R covers the external pointer and\nthe symbol case.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/393,\nwhere CI results can be seen.",
            "creation_time": "2026-10-21T16:38:36Z"
          },
